<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 vehicle exports down 2.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 vehicle exports down 2.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle exports fell 2.1 percent in calendar 1996 from a year earlier to 3,711,454 units, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association (JAMA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was the 11th successive yearly fall.</p>
<p>The association also said Japan's vehicle exports in December rose 1.1 percent from a year earlier to 317,833 units, the seventh successive month that exports had risen on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the data for 1996, with percentage changes:</p>
<p>			    1996	    YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Cars		    2,860,080	down  1.2 pct</p>
<p> Trucks		    807,508	down  5.0 pct</p>
<p> Buses			43,866	down  1.9 pct</p>
<p>1996 exports by destination:</p>
<p> Asia			620,016	up    0.6 pct</p>
<p> Mideast		   284,881	up   38.0 pct</p>
<p> Europe		    948,712	up    3.3 pct</p>
<p> - EU			801,858	up    1.2 pct</p>
<p> North America	 1,169,073	down 10.2 pct</p>
<p> - U.S.		  1,098,504	down 10.6 pct</p>
<p> Latin America	   279,641	down 15.0 pct</p>
<p> Oceania		   265,478	down  3.4 pct</p>
<p> Africa		    134,027	down  2.7 pct</p>
<p> Other			 9,626	up   44.2 pct</p>
<p>1996 exports by Japanese manufacturers:</p>
<p> Toyota     1,276,662	up    6.2 pct</p>
<p> Nissan	 581,854	down  2.7 pct</p>
<p> Mitsubishi   455,498	down 10.0 pct</p>
<p> Mazda	  454,125	up    3.1 pct</p>
<p> Honda	  371,174	down 14.5 pct</p>
<p> Suzuki	 189,788	down  5.4 pct</p>
<p> Isuzu	  186,408	down 10.5 pct</p>
<p> Fuji Heavy    80,610	up   13.0 pct</p>
<p> Daihatsu	63,003	down 17.1 pct</p>
<p> Hino Motors   30,888	down  1.2 pct</p>
<p> Nissan Diesel 21,444	down  4.2 pct</p>
